※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ `_` takes every alternative no earlier arm took, and binds nothing: the
※ alternatives it takes may carry different things or nothing at all, so there
※ is no one value a name after it could stand for.  It works on every kind of
※ value a `match` takes apart.

let hundred: mut u8 = 100u8
let none: mut u8 = 0u8
let seven: mut u8 = 7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let kept: mut u8 = 0u8
    ※ a wildcard beside a named arm
    match hundred ÷ seven:
        u8(q):
            kept ← q
        _:
            kept ← 1u8
    ※ and one taking both, so there is nothing to ask and nothing to branch on
    match hundred ÷ none:
        _:
            kept ← kept + 50u8
    ※ what this used to say through the exit status, which is six bits now
    if kept ≠ 64u8:
        1u6
    else:
        0u6
